   "note": "not found as stated: no ELB page in the corpus says in one sentence that a load balancer is a Regional resource. Looked in userguide/disaster-recovery-resiliency, userguide/how-elastic-load-balancing-works, userguide/what-is-load-balancing, application/introduction, network/introduction, application/application-load-balancers and the ELB FAQ (grep 'regional', 'region'). Closest evidence: load balancers span the Availability Zones you enable, and AWS Global Accelerator is the way to spread traffic across load balancers in one or more Regions. Writers must not state 'Regional' as a hard fact without a new source."
